-- A QA checklist attached to a task: the concrete, human-checkable things to test on this
-- task's change. It is GENERATED by the pull-request agent when «Створити ПР» runs, and
-- TICKED OFF by a human (a tester or a manager) on the board.
--
-- It lives on the task, NOT on the session, on purpose: a session's «archive» is a local
-- hide flag (SupervisorService.setArchived) that never touches the cloud, so a checklist kept
-- on the session would vanish from the board the moment the work is filed away. On the task it
-- outlives the session and is readable by exactly the members who can read the card.
--
-- Shape (mirrors @kermanych/core's QaChecklist):
--   { "generatedAt": iso, "sessionId": "...", "items": [ { "id","text","checked",
--     "checkedBy"?, "checkedAt"? } ] }
-- `{}` (the default) is «no checklist yet» — toTask() maps an item-less object to an absent key.
--
-- jsonb, `not null default '{}'`, exactly like every additive task column before it
-- (20260831090000_task_effort.sql, 20260904100000_task_hidden.sql): the table-level grants in
-- 20260821090200 and the row-predicated tasks policies / tasks_guard() cover the new column the
-- moment it exists. Ticking an item is an ordinary member UPDATE — not a status or assignee
-- change — so tasks_guard() lets any project member (the tester) write it.
alter table public.tasks
  add column if not exists qa_checklist jsonb not null default '{}'::jsonb;
